Repair the complete CommonJS source below and return a corrected complete source file exporting exactly `{ resizeTextRuns }`.

`resizeTextRuns(runs, pointSize)` must accept an array of records shaped as `{ text, pointSize }` and an absolute target size. Every `text` must be a string and every existing size must be finite; malformed records throw `TypeError`. The target must be a finite number from 1 through 500 inclusive; a non-number or non-finite value throws `TypeError`, while an out-of-range value throws `RangeError`. Return a new array with every run set to the target size. Preserve ordering and text exactly. An empty array returns an empty array. Do not mutate the array or its records, and do not retain record aliases.

Known-bad source:
```javascript
function resizeTextRuns(runs, pointSize) {
  if (!Array.isArray(runs)) throw new TypeError('Runs must be an array');
  if (typeof pointSize !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(pointSize)) {
    throw new TypeError('Point size must be finite');
  }
  if (pointSize < 1 || pointSize > 500) throw new RangeError('Point size out of range');
  return runs.map((run) => {
    if (!run || typeof run !== 'object' || typeof run.text !== 'string' || !Number.isFinite(run.pointSize)) {
      throw new TypeError('Invalid text run');
    }
    return { text: run.text, pointSize: run.pointSize + pointSize };
  });
}

module.exports = { resizeTextRuns };
```

